## Flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here.
##
## A smaller allocator footprint. Measured 2026-11-28 on a fresh boot after
## collecting every process: allocator carriers 253 to 224 MB, erlang:memory
## total 260 to 236 MB. Each scheduler owns an instance of every allocator, so
## fewer schedulers leave fewer half-empty carriers. A dev daemon (mix run)
## takes the same set through ERL_FLAGS; see the compos-boot skill.

## four normal schedulers, two dirty CPU, four dirty IO
+S 4:4
+SDcpu 2:2
+SDio 4

## address-order best fit and smaller carriers, so freed memory goes back
## to the OS instead of idling in a 5 MB carrier
+MBas aobf
+MHas aobf
+MBlmbcs 512
+MHlmbcs 512
+MBsmbcs 128
+MHsmbcs 128

## a full sweep every 20 minor collections, so old binaries go sooner
-env ERL_FULLSWEEP_AFTER 20
